encies]`. Note the crates registry is unreachable from the sandbox — **use `cargo test --offline`**; the needed `.crate` files were already in the local cargo cache.\n- `.cargo/config.toml` (new): sets `RUST_TEST_THREADS = \"1\"`. This is required, not cosmetic — the harness redirects process-global fd 1, so parallel tests leaked libtest's own progress output into captures (11 spurious failures before this).\n\n## Notes\n- No binary/driver executable exists (`CMakeLists.txt` has only `add_library`, `Cargo.toml` only `cdylib`), so the stdout-comparison gate for binaries is N/A — but stdout is compared byte-for-byte on every row anyway.\n- `Cargo.toml` declares no `[features]`, so the default set is the only feature configuration.\n- `bad`/`good` share an address in the Rust release build (identical-code folding). Both symbols are still exported and independently `dlsym`-able; a test asserts this rather than relying on the addresses differing.\n- `bad()`'s intentional 40-into-10-bytes overflow prints `0` in both, confirmed over 1000 consecutive calls without corruption."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":638,"cache_read_input_tokens":56457,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":638,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5bcc284a-49f8-4219-8e0a-c130a7150da7","uuid":"5ab293f2-f729-4673-b442-dda01b9d3e32","timestamp":"2026-09-05T03:48:46.431Z"}
